lines[20]:
  - i, text, start, end
  - 0, "In 1914, a couple in Idaho mailed their five year old daughter", 0.3, 5.187
  - 1, to her grandma's house., 5.187, 6.541
  - 2, With the stamps stuck right on her coat., 6.721, 8.483
  - 3, "See, the post office had just started delivering packages,", 8.663, 11.953
  - 4, "and May's parents wanted her to visit grandma,", 12.373, 14.623
  - 5, seventy-three miles away., 15.083, 16.787
  - 6, But a train ticket wasn't cheap., 16.967, 18.719
  - 7, So her dad walked her into the post office, 18.899, 21.549
  - 8, and asked how much it costs to mail a kid., 21.729, 23.953
  - 9, "The clerk checked the rules,", 24.133, 25.503
  - 10, and nothing said he couldn't., 25.803, 27.019
  - 11, "May weighed forty-eight and a half pounds,", 27.199, 29.359
  - 12, just under the fifty pound limit., 29.739, 31.37
  - 13, "So on went fifty-three cents in stamps,", 31.55, 33.86
  - 14, "and she rode the train in the mail car,", 33.96, 36.37
  - 15, "with her mom's cousin, who happened to be the mail clerk.", 36.78, 39.782
  - 16, He walked her right up to grandma's front door., 39.962, 42.402
  - 17, "Soon after, the post office banned mailing people.", 42.582, 45.395
  - 18, "Which is why today, you can still mail baby chicks,", 45.575, 48.765
  - 19, but not your little sister., 49.025, 50.223
